r>
&gt; summarized in regular documents to reserve them, so that they are<br>
&gt; ultimately reflected in the registries. A new document every six weeks=
 is<br>
&gt; probably impractical, but we can batch them up.<br>
&gt; <br>
&gt; We are interested in the community=E2=80=99s feedback on this proposal=
=E2=80=94anyone who<br>
&gt; might participate, better safeguards, or thoughts on the mechanism as =
a<br>
&gt; whole. We hope it will help the working group evolve its protocols mor=
e<br>
&gt; smoothly in the future.<br>
<br>
</span>This looks interesting and I very much agree that we should do *somt=
hing* to<br>
try to avoid the pain we&#39;ve seen with deploying TLS 1.3 for future vers=
ions.<br>
<br>
We (Cloudflare) would be happy to help with developing and deploying it, an=
d<br>
see how the experiment goes (and maybe even help put a draft together if ne=
eded,<br>
if that is the form this proposal will take).<br>
<br>
Cheers<br>
